1
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:14,767
What's going on?

2
00:00:16,667 --> 00:00:17,933
Well...

3
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,167
Um...

4
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,800
Pretending you didn't see me?

5
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,743
That's cold, don't you think?

6
00:00:35,767 --> 00:00:37,000
Wait!

7
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:41,233
Hinata didn't show up today either.
Did something happen?

8
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:45,900
Sora Senpai...

9
00:00:47,667 --> 00:00:48,833
Wait up!

10
00:00:57,133 --> 00:01:01,267
♪ Ups and downs every single day ♪

11
00:01:01,367 --> 00:01:05,033
♪ Time just keeps slipping away ♪

12
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:08,867
♪ This love has grown way past friendship ♪

13
00:01:08,967 --> 00:01:12,033
♪ This must be what love feels like ♪

14
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:15,267
♪ This is my love ♪

15
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:17,600
♪ Walking up the campus slope ♪

16
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:22,833
♪ We were just nameless strangers ♪

17
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:24,967
♪ All the people passing by ♪

18
00:01:25,067 --> 00:01:30,100
♪ Running toward different tomorrows ♪

19
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:33,933
♪ Meeting you that summer ♪

20
00:01:34,033 --> 00:01:37,133
♪ Turned the wheels of fate ♪

21
00:01:37,233 --> 00:01:42,867
♪ Took the leap, yet
still questioning myself ♪

22
00:01:42,967 --> 00:01:43,533
♪ Can't find the words ♪

23
00:01:43,633 --> 00:01:47,800
♪ If this is love, it's so hard to say ♪

24
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:51,500
♪ What kind of face will
you show tomorrow? ♪

25
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:56,700
♪ We're so much more than friends now ♪

26
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,767
♪ This is definitely love ♪

27
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:01,633
"Your Sky Hare nochi Koi"

28
00:02:07,400 --> 00:02:08,543
[Episode 9: The Story of the Sky and the Sun]
Who is he talking to?

29
00:02:08,567 --> 00:02:10,233
I can't see!

30
00:02:10,333 --> 00:02:11,567
Stop pushing!

31
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:15,500
Have you been in touch
with Hinata since then?

32
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:16,800
No.

33
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:19,700
I see.

34
00:02:21,567 --> 00:02:23,100
It's not just Hinata.

35
00:02:23,736 --> 00:02:25,936
I hurt his family, too.

36
00:02:28,267 --> 00:02:29,333
So I just...

37
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:30,724
Can you only wait?

38
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,600
You really do have a soft side.

39
00:02:39,667 --> 00:02:44,733
Hinata is sensitive and stubborn.

40
00:02:44,833 --> 00:02:49,924
If you leave him alone, he
might never sort out how he feels.

41
00:03:12,083 --> 00:03:13,651
[W/ Sora: I'll wait for you at my place tomorrow
at 4:00 PM!] [Okay. No matter how they react,]

42
00:03:13,675 --> 00:03:16,115
[I'll figure something out.
Don't worry.] [Thank you, Senpai!]

43
00:03:22,767 --> 00:03:24,233
I miss him so much.

44
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,967
Stay away from my son!

45
00:03:30,667 --> 00:03:32,800
I put Senpai through so much pain.

46
00:03:34,533 --> 00:03:37,100
It's my fault for not
saying something sooner.

47
00:03:38,367 --> 00:03:40,000
It's all my fault.

48
00:03:42,433 --> 00:03:43,700
Hinata?

49
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,100
Dinner's ready!

50
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:49,133
Hinata?

51
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,000
He's an adult now.

52
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,267
Just leave him be.

53
00:04:12,100 --> 00:04:15,033
I understand where you're coming from.

54
00:04:15,867 --> 00:04:19,467
But acting like that is only hurting him.

55
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:24,867
Why not sit down and
have a proper talk with him?

56
00:04:24,967 --> 00:04:26,967
All I want is for Hinata

57
00:04:27,067 --> 00:04:31,167
to be with someone kind,
someone who'll support him.

58
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:35,333
So you don't think Sora is kind?

59
00:04:35,433 --> 00:04:36,233
That guy...

60
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:39,067
You haven't even had a
real conversation with him,

61
00:04:39,167 --> 00:04:40,309
and you've already written him off.

62
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:43,033
I just don't want Hinata
to do something he'll regret later.

63
00:04:43,133 --> 00:04:45,400
Isn't that just your own fear talking?

64
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:49,886
Hinata looked so genuinely happy.

65
00:04:51,642 --> 00:04:56,042
Can't you take a good, hard look
at your own son?

66
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:33,500
I really want to see him.

67
00:06:03,867 --> 00:06:07,867
I knew it. I have to go see him.

68
00:06:25,396 --> 00:06:30,629
If you just leave him alone, Hinata
might stay trapped like this forever.

69
00:06:35,500 --> 00:06:36,867
Bro?

70
00:06:40,033 --> 00:06:41,333
Sora-san?

71
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:46,700
Hanamura Sora-san!

72
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:51,100
I have to go to him.

73
00:06:51,767 --> 00:06:53,033
Huh?

74
00:06:56,567 --> 00:06:57,867
So pure.

75
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,167
Are you all right?

76
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:24,067
Can you move?

77
00:07:27,867 --> 00:07:29,300
I'll call an ambulance.

78
00:07:32,233 --> 00:07:33,600
I need an ambulance, please.

79
00:07:34,300 --> 00:07:37,267
A woman collapsed on the
roadside, and she can't move.

80
00:07:38,467 --> 00:07:39,500
Yes.

81
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:41,667
She's conscious.

82
00:07:44,567 --> 00:07:46,767
On the street next to 1-chome Park.

83
00:07:46,867 --> 00:07:47,967
Understood.

84
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:49,767
Please hurry.

85
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:52,900
Are you holding up?

86
00:07:56,033 --> 00:07:57,033
Sora...

87
00:07:57,233 --> 00:08:00,500
[Funase Residence]

88
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:06,100
Can you hear me?

89
00:08:06,133 --> 00:08:08,400
Can you tell me your name?

90
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:14,267
We'll brief you once
the procedure is finished.

91
00:08:14,367 --> 00:08:15,667
Please wait here.

92
00:08:17,733 --> 00:08:21,100
[X-Ray Check-in]

93
00:08:42,633 --> 00:08:44,033
Have a seat.

94
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:04,767
Here you go.

95
00:09:42,233 --> 00:09:43,600
What do we do...

96
00:09:46,833 --> 00:09:48,067
What should we do...

97
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:50,800
It's all right.

98
00:09:53,567 --> 00:09:55,000
She's going to be fine.

99
00:09:58,467 --> 00:10:01,667
She's been moved to a ward to rest.

100
00:10:02,733 --> 00:10:05,033
There's no serious harm this time.

101
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:10,400
However, she will need
to stay hospitalized for a bit

102
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:12,400
so we can keep her under observation.

103
00:10:13,567 --> 00:10:14,900
Understood.

104
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,233
Thank you, Doctor.

105
00:10:16,967 --> 00:10:18,800
Thank goodness.

106
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:55,467
Your name is Sora, right?

107
00:10:59,067 --> 00:11:00,433
I'm Hanamura Sora.

108
00:11:00,533 --> 00:11:03,300
I'm terribly sorry I didn't
introduce myself properly last time.

109
00:11:13,467 --> 00:11:14,867
Sit.

110
00:11:15,433 --> 00:11:16,633
Yes, sir.

111
00:11:18,267 --> 00:11:19,467
Excuse me.

112
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,567
Hinata told me everything.

113
00:11:28,067 --> 00:11:29,967
Thanks to you, his mother was saved.

114
00:11:31,467 --> 00:11:32,900
Thank you.

115
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:39,033
However, that's completely separate.

116
00:11:42,933 --> 00:11:44,433
I told you the other day,

117
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:48,333
stop treating relationships like a game.

118
00:11:49,033 --> 00:11:50,300
This isn't a game to me.

119
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:57,700
All I want is for you
to build a normal family.

120
00:11:57,800 --> 00:12:02,033
I want to be with Senpai!

121
00:12:05,467 --> 00:12:07,600
You don't understand anything.

122
00:12:08,967 --> 00:12:12,233
You just go with the flow,

123
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,667
without a shred of responsibility.

124
00:12:17,733 --> 00:12:19,733
When will you grow up?

125
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:26,300
Is being true to my feelings
really irresponsible?

126
00:12:28,033 --> 00:12:32,133
Is it wrong to want to
be with the one I love?

127
00:12:34,700 --> 00:12:36,267
If that's the case,

128
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:39,767
then I never want to grow up!

129
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,033
Hinata...

130
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:58,233
If you think saving his mother means
I have to approve of your relationship,

131
00:12:59,100 --> 00:13:01,333
it's not that simple.

132
00:13:04,133 --> 00:13:05,400
I know.

133
00:13:07,833 --> 00:13:10,967
I didn't do it to win your approval.

134
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,567
Someone precious to me was in trouble,

135
00:13:16,667 --> 00:13:18,367
so I wanted to be close to them.

136
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:23,400
Someone precious, huh?

137
00:13:25,833 --> 00:13:29,733
Hinata is, and so is his family.

138
00:13:38,267 --> 00:13:40,067
I want to be with Hinata.

139
00:13:40,867 --> 00:13:42,633
And that's something I won't back down on.

140
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:55,000
I hear you're already in the workforce.

141
00:13:55,267 --> 00:13:56,433
Yes, sir.

142
00:13:57,133 --> 00:13:59,367
You're quite different from Hinata.

143
00:13:59,467 --> 00:14:01,400
No, Hinata...

144
00:14:04,867 --> 00:14:07,633
Hinata brings happiness
to everyone around him.

145
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:12,900
He can do things that I never could.

146
00:14:15,867 --> 00:14:20,600
Oh? I thought you were
supposed to make him happy?

147
00:14:35,867 --> 00:14:37,967
[Funase Residence]

148
00:14:44,833 --> 00:14:46,467
[Welcome Home from the Hospital]

149
00:14:56,633 --> 00:14:57,833
Ah.

150
00:14:59,733 --> 00:15:01,067
Honestly...

151
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:05,567
[Aimi: Almost there]

152
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:11,333
Come on, step inside.

153
00:15:11,433 --> 00:15:12,733
Thank you.

154
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,500
I'm home!

155
00:15:16,900 --> 00:15:18,700
Surprise!

156
00:15:19,467 --> 00:15:21,033
Goodness, you startled me!

157
00:15:21,133 --> 00:15:22,433
Welcome home!

158
00:15:22,900 --> 00:15:23,967
I'm back.

159
00:15:24,067 --> 00:15:25,433
Come in, come on in!

160
00:15:28,267 --> 00:15:29,533
What is all this?

161
00:15:29,633 --> 00:15:30,900
What's going on?

162
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:31,667
Well,

163
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:34,533
since we couldn't properly
celebrate your birthday last time...

164
00:15:36,367 --> 00:15:38,567
Dad suggested it, actually.

165
00:15:39,133 --> 00:15:44,067
So I begged Senpai
to whip up this amazing feast.

166
00:15:48,400 --> 00:15:50,200
Congratulations on leaving the hospital.

167
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:53,533
Thank you.

168
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:57,400
Here, take a seat.

169
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,567
Thank you.

170
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:06,267
What's up? Something on your mind?

171
00:16:06,367 --> 00:16:11,633
Dad really loves Mom, doesn't he?

172
00:16:13,433 --> 00:16:14,767
Huh?

173
00:16:14,867 --> 00:16:15,933
Where did that come from?

174
00:16:16,033 --> 00:16:19,233
I guess I've always taken it for granted.

175
00:16:19,667 --> 00:16:21,700
I hope I can have what you share...

176
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:27,633
just like Mom and Dad.

177
00:16:35,733 --> 00:16:37,033
Sora.

178
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:39,233
Hinata.

179
00:16:42,433 --> 00:16:43,733
Congratulations.

180
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:50,433
Thank you.

181
00:16:50,533 --> 00:16:52,000
Thank you, sir.

182
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:54,167
Today is about celebrating Mom coming home!

183
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:55,633
- Let's dig in.
- All right.

184
00:16:55,733 --> 00:16:56,500
Eat up, everyone!

185
00:16:56,600 --> 00:16:57,833
- You too, Sora.
- Okay.

186
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,809
- It looks so good!
- It really does!

187
00:16:59,833 --> 00:17:01,073
- Who wants a small plate?
- Me!

188
00:17:01,167 --> 00:17:02,167
Here you go.

189
00:17:05,967 --> 00:17:08,400
Whoa... what is up with those two?

190
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:09,509
They look so good together.

191
00:17:09,533 --> 00:17:10,933
Wait, pause it right there.

192
00:17:11,033 --> 00:17:11,767
Right here, look!

193
00:17:11,867 --> 00:17:13,176
- Wait, then what?
- This is so good!

194
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:13,800
Hold on.

195
00:17:13,900 --> 00:17:14,767
What's gonna happen?

196
00:17:14,867 --> 00:17:16,667
Hey! Wait, wait!

197
00:17:17,667 --> 00:17:18,967
What happens next?

198
00:17:19,833 --> 00:17:21,509
Am I the only one
actually working here?

199
00:17:21,533 --> 00:17:24,733
Didn't you ask us to help out
since the manager is away?

200
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:25,567
Yeah, exactly!

201
00:17:25,667 --> 00:17:27,467
None of you are helping at all!

202
00:17:28,333 --> 00:17:29,200
Look at you guys.

203
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:31,533
You're all just lounging around.

204
00:17:31,633 --> 00:17:34,833
Fine, fine, I'll help you out.

205
00:17:35,733 --> 00:17:36,900
What needs doing?

206
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,833
So, did you two end up dating or not?

207
00:17:40,933 --> 00:17:42,333
- Yes.
- No.

208
00:17:42,567 --> 00:17:44,500
Wait, hold on.

209
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,160
Are you guys still playing hard to get?

210
00:17:46,567 --> 00:17:48,400
Still wooing him~.

211
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,167
Still letting him chase me~.

212
00:17:50,900 --> 00:17:52,067
That's so weird.

213
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:59,633
What about you two? What's your status?

214
00:18:01,133 --> 00:18:03,367
What do you mean, 'what's our status'?

215
00:18:09,900 --> 00:18:12,600
We started dating last week.

216
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:14,567
- Congrats!
- Congratulations!

217
00:18:16,267 --> 00:18:19,067
So that's that.

218
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:25,600
Just please don't tell my brother yet.

219
00:18:27,167 --> 00:18:28,300
I heard that.

220
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:30,533
When did you get here?

221
00:18:31,667 --> 00:18:33,933
Looks like Riku found a great partner too.

222
00:18:34,367 --> 00:18:37,167
Well...

223
00:18:37,267 --> 00:18:38,609
Riku, that face is totally unfair!

224
00:18:38,633 --> 00:18:40,733
Ah, did I use to make
that kind of face too?

225
00:18:40,833 --> 00:18:42,333
All the time~.

226
00:18:43,867 --> 00:18:45,000
Aimi.

227
00:18:46,567 --> 00:18:47,167
- Go out with—
- No.

228
00:18:47,267 --> 00:18:48,167
Huh?

229
00:18:48,267 --> 00:18:50,300
Zero hesitation. It's a no.

230
00:18:50,400 --> 00:18:52,509
- Come on, at least think about it!
- Thought about it, still no.

231
00:18:52,533 --> 00:18:53,633
We're done.

232
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:56,167
I'm ruined.

233
00:18:56,267 --> 00:18:57,433
Ruito~.

234
00:18:58,733 --> 00:18:59,733
Don't be sad.

235
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,300
I'm the only single one left!

236
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:03,240
- There, there, don't cry.
- How is this fair?!

237
00:19:24,667 --> 00:19:26,500
I am your sky,

238
00:19:26,599 --> 00:19:28,699
and you are my sunshine.

239
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,667
That's Hinata and me.

240
00:19:33,767 --> 00:19:35,733
The sky and the sun...

241
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:38,033
have finally met.

242
00:19:42,500 --> 00:19:48,100
Senpai really is... just like the sky.

243
00:20:17,667 --> 00:20:19,500
You are my sky,

244
00:20:19,733 --> 00:20:23,333
and I am your sunshine.

245
00:21:17,167 --> 00:21:19,267
It smells like you, Senpai.

246
00:21:21,067 --> 00:21:22,633
Of course it does.

247
00:22:31,467 --> 00:22:32,800
Senpai.

248
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:34,700
Yeah?

249
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:08,433
Thank you so much for watching the
final episode of "Your Sky Hare nochi Koi!"

250
00:25:08,533 --> 00:25:10,233
Thank you, everyone!

251
00:25:10,667 --> 00:25:12,043
Thank you all for
watching until the very end!

252
00:25:12,067 --> 00:25:13,133
Thank you!

253
00:25:13,800 --> 00:25:15,167
How did you like it?

254
00:25:15,267 --> 00:25:17,600
So much has happened!

255
00:25:17,700 --> 00:25:20,000
But in the end, at the beach...

256
00:25:20,100 --> 00:25:20,867
we had such a blast.

257
00:25:20,967 --> 00:25:21,300
Refreshing!

258
00:25:21,400 --> 00:25:21,867
Oh!

259
00:25:22,100 --> 00:25:22,733
Exhilarating!

260
00:25:22,833 --> 00:25:23,833
Oh!

261
00:25:23,933 --> 00:25:25,867
From here on, a bright future awaits.

262
00:25:25,967 --> 00:25:26,867
Yes.

263
00:25:26,967 --> 00:25:28,567
- Even Dad came around.
- Exactly.

264
00:25:29,233 --> 00:25:34,200
A huge thank you to everyone
who stuck with us this far!

265
00:25:34,300 --> 00:25:34,933
Truly.

266
00:25:35,033 --> 00:25:36,600
Thank you for showing us so much love!

267
00:25:36,700 --> 00:25:38,733
- Thank you all so very much!
- Thank you!

268
00:25:40,300 --> 00:25:44,033
We hope to see you all again
somewhere down the road.

269
00:25:44,933 --> 00:25:46,076
Be sure to catch us when we do!

270
00:25:46,100 --> 00:25:47,200
It's a promise!

271
00:25:47,300 --> 00:25:48,433
Bye-bye~.

272
00:25:48,533 --> 00:25:49,867
Thank you, everyone!

273
00:25:53,633 --> 00:25:54,633
Your Sky Hare nochi Koi
